CLIMATELENS INDIA
DATASET SOURCES AND REFERENCES
==============================================

PROJECT: ClimateLens India
LIBRARY: NIElytics
TOTAL DATASETS: 7

==============================================
1. LANDSLIDES - INDIA LANDSLIDE DATASET
==============================================

Dataset Name: India Landslide CSV
Filename: landslide_data_india.csv

Source: riseuppant, GitHub
Repository: Disaster_Management
Format: CSV
Coverage: India

Citation:
riseuppant. (n.d.). India Landslide Dataset
[CSV dataset]. GitHub.

Dataset Source:
https://github.com/riseuppant/Disaster_Management/blob/main/landslide_data_india.csv

Direct Download:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/riseuppant/Disaster_Management/main/landslide_data_india.csv

Purpose:
Used to analyze historical landslide occurrences
and visualize landslide locations across India.

Note:
This is a community-hosted dataset. Its original
scientific source has not been verified.


==============================================
2. INDIA BOUNDARIES - STATE BOUNDARY DATASET
==============================================

Dataset Name: State Boundary GeoJSON
Filename: state_nwic_geojson.zip

Source: National Water Informatics Centre (NWIC)
Organization: Ministry of Jal Shakti,
Government of India
Format: ZIP (GeoJSON)
Coverage: All Indian States and Union Territories

Citation:
National Water Informatics Centre. (2025).
State Boundary [Geospatial dataset].
National Water Data Portal, Government of India.

Dataset Source:
https://nwdp.nwic.gov.in/dataset/dd960900-34cc-4486-a95c-83200d2f2c7b

Direct Download:
https://nwdp.nwic.gov.in/dataset/dd960900-34cc-4486-a95c-83200d2f2c7b/resource/f039e721-132c-4a24-9e5e-07af03064b4d/download/state_nwic_geojson.zip

Purpose:
Used to display the interactive India map,
identify state boundaries, and visualize
state-wise climate and disaster information.


==============================================
3. DROUGHT - HISTORICAL NATIONAL DROUGHT DATA
==============================================

Dataset Name: India Drought Area Time Series
Filename: India_Drought_Area_Timeseries.txt

Source: India Drought Monitor
Organization: Water and Climate Lab,
Indian Institute of Technology Gandhinagar
Format: TXT
Coverage: India

Citation:
Water and Climate Lab, IIT Gandhinagar. (n.d.).
India Drought Monitor - National Drought Area
Time Series [TXT dataset].
Indian Institute of Technology Gandhinagar.

Official Website:
https://indiadroughtmonitor.in/

Dataset Source:
https://indiadroughtmonitor.in/data-download.html

Direct Download:
https://indiadroughtmonitor.in/data/India_Drought_Area_Timeseries.txt

Purpose:
Used to analyze historical drought patterns,
monitor changes in drought-affected areas,
and study drought severity across India.

Note:
The selected time series is national-level data.
It does not independently provide district-wise
drought severity.


==============================================
4. HEAT - HISTORICAL MAXIMUM TEMPERATURE DATA
==============================================

Dataset Name: Historical India Maximum Temperature
Filename: NEW-TXREGION.TXT

Source: Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology
Organization: IITM Pune / India Meteorological
Department (IMD)
Format: TXT
Coverage: India and climatic regions
Time Period: 1901-2007

Citation:
Indian Institute of Tropical Meteorology. (2012).
IITM Indian Regional Monthly Surface Air
Temperature Dataset: All-India and Regional
Maximum Temperatures (1901-2007)
[TXT dataset]. IITM Pune.

Direct Download:
https://www.tropmet.res.in/data/data-archival/txtn/NEW-TXREGION.TXT

Dataset Documentation:
https://www.tropmet.res.in/data/data-archival/txtn/README.pdf

Purpose:
Used to analyze historical maximum-temperature
patterns, identify long-term warming trends,
and compare regional temperature variations.

Note:
Monthly temperature records are suitable for
climate trend analysis but are insufficient
for identifying individual daily heatwave events.


